            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0619" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/2905: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                        France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-01T19:00:00-04:00">September 1, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>B–15. Your 79, August 29, 3 p.m., and your 83, August 31, 4 p.m.<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d458-f1"/> In a separate telegram I have requested you to telegraph
                    the text of the recommendations of the diplomatic corps to render more humane
                    the conflict in Spain. In your reply please let us know whether there has been
                    any change in the procedure set forth in your 79 of August 29, 3 p.m., whereby
                    the Spanish Government would be consulted as to whether it has any objection to
                    the submission of the same proposal to the rebel leaders.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d458-f1" n="64" xml:id="d458-f1-content">
